items: ci-status-guard-desc-green-always-red
paths: tests/e2e/ci-status-guard.sh scripts/ci-status
scope: |
  `Validate ScalaScript` is red on EVERY CI run, and not on ScalaScript: it fails its own
  self-test `ci-status-guard[desc-green]` with `expected exit=0 got=2`. The guard uses a FAKE
  gh, so this is not about real CI throughput — the reported SHA is printed as
  `<sha>~5` with the suffix UNRESOLVED, which points at rev-parse resolving `${DESC_SHA}~5`
  differently in CI than locally (shallow checkout is the obvious candidate; measure, do not assume).
  Fix the guard so it is honest under both checkout depths, without weakening the negative case
  that keeps the descendant fallback from accepting any recent run as evidence.
next: reproduce locally against a shallow clone, then fix
